-- title:
--   Oriented crossing chart of X₁(Mp) over a valuation subring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$, $M \neq 0$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L((q))$, assumed (hypothesis `hK`) to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational function field of $X_1(Mp)$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$.
--
--   Coefficient data: $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with a fraction-field structure $A \hookrightarrow L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAp`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$; $\varpi \in A$ is a generator of the maximal ideal (`hϖ`). Further, $j$ is a nonzero element of $K$ whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant (`hj`). The scheme under consideration is the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) over $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   Special-fibre data: $k$ is an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with an $A$-algebra structure. $C_1, C_2$ are schemes with structure morphisms $c_1, c_2$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k$ that are proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and $i_1, i_2$ are morphisms over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ from $C_1$, $C_2$ to the base change $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathrm{modelTo}, \operatorname{Spec}(A \to k))$ of the two-chart model to $k$ (elements of `SchemeHomOver`, i.e. morphisms whose composite with the structure morphism of the base change is $c_1$, resp. $c_2$), both closed immersions. The hypothesis `hcover` states that every point of that base change lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred` states that the scheme-theoretic intersection $\mathrm{pullback}(i_1, i_2)$ is reduced, and `hn`, `hn0` record that its number of points equals $n$ with $0 < n$.
--
--   Valuation-subring data: $Pl$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ with `Pl.LiesOverPrime p`, that is, $p$ is a nonunit of $Pl$; the algebra structures of $A$ and $L$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ form a tower. A ring homomorphism $\rho : A \to Pl$ is given with $\rho$ followed by the inclusion $Pl \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equal to the structure map of $A$ (`hρ`), and a surjective ring homomorphism $\pi_k : Pl \to k$ with $\pi_k \circ \rho$ equal to the structure map $A \to k$ (`hAlgk`, `hπk`). A morphism $bc$ from the base change of the two-chart model along $A \to k$ to its base change along $\rho$ is given, commuting with the projections to the model (`hbc₁`) and satisfying $bc$ followed by the second projection equal to the second projection followed by $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k)$ (`hbc₂`).
--
--   Intermediate coefficient ring: $O$ is a discrete valuation domain with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O : A \to O$ and an injective ring homomorphism $\iota : O \to Pl$ such that $\iota \circ \rho_O = \rho$ (`hι`, `hιinj`), $\iota$ reflects and preserves the maximal ideals ($\iota(o)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $Pl$ iff $o$ lies in that of $O$, `hιloc`), the composite $o \mapsto \pi_k(\iota(o))$ is surjective onto $k$ (`hιsurj`), and (`hιfix`) every $\tau$ in the decomposition subgroup of $Pl$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ which lies in the inertia subgroup and fixes the image of $L$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ pointwise satisfies $\tau \cdot \iota(o) = \iota(o)$ for all $o \in O$. A morphism $bc_O$ from the base change along $A \to k$ to the base change along $\rho_O$ is given, with the same two compatibilities as $bc$, the second one through $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k \circ \iota)$ (`hbcO₁`, `hbcO₂`).
--
--   The chart over $O$: let $\nu$ be a point of $\mathrm{pullback}(i_1, i_2)$ and write $x_\nu$ for its image under the first projection followed by $i_1$ followed by $bc_O$. Let $e \ge 1$, let $U_0$ be an open subscheme of the base change along $\rho_O$ containing $x_\nu$ (`hxU₀`), and let $f_0 : U_0 \to \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[u,v]/(uv - \rho_O(\varpi)^e)\bigr)$, the crossing scheme `CrossingQuotient.crossingScheme ((ρO ϖ) ^ e)`, be a morphism subject to: `hover₀`, $f_0$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $O \to O[u,v]/(uv-\rho_O(\varpi)^e)$ equals the open immersion $U_0 \hookrightarrow$ base change followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} O$; `hfib₀`, for $y \in U_0$ both distinguished coordinate classes `CrossingQuotient.U` and `CrossingQuotient.V` lie in the prime $f_0(y)$ precisely when $y$ maps to $x_\nu$; `hpt₀`, at every $y$ over $x_\nu$ the stalk map of $f_0$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal, and induces an isomorphism of residue fields; `het₀`, every such $y$ has an open neighbourhood $V$ in $U_0$ with $V \hookrightarrow U_0$ followed by $f_0$ étale; and the orientation hypotheses `hor₁`–`hor₄`: for $y \in U_0$, `CrossingQuotient.V` lies in $f_0(y)$ iff the image of $y$ lies in the image of $i_1$ followed by $bc_O$, and `CrossingQuotient.U` lies in $f_0(y)$ iff that image lies in the image of $i_2$ followed by $bc_O$ (each direction being a separate clause).
--
--   Conclusion. Write $x'_\nu$ for the image of $\nu$ under the first projection of $\mathrm{pullback}(i_1,i_2)$ followed by $i_1$ followed by $bc$, a point of the base change of the two-chart model along $\rho$. Then there exist an open subscheme $U$ of that base change with $x'_\nu \in U$, and a morphism $f : U \to \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(Pl[u,v]/(uv - \rho(\varpi)^e)\bigr)$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (1) $f$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $Pl \to Pl[u,v]/(uv-\rho(\varpi)^e)$ equals the open immersion $U \hookrightarrow$ base change followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} Pl$.
--
--   (2) For every $y \in U$: both `CrossingQuotient.U ((ρ ϖ) ^ e)` and `CrossingQuotient.V ((ρ ϖ) ^ e)` lie in the prime ideal $f(y)$ if and only if $y$ maps to $x'_\nu$.
--
--   (3) For every $y \in U$ mapping to $x'_\nu$: the stalk map of $f$ at $y$ is flat, the image ideal of the maximal ideal under the stalk map equals the maximal ideal, and the induced map of residue fields is an isomorphism.
--
--   (4) There is an open $W \subseteq U$ containing some $y$ that maps to $x'_\nu$, such that $W \hookrightarrow U$ followed by $f$ is étale.
--
--   (5) Inertia equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the decomposition subgroup of $Pl$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ which lies in the inertia subgroup and fixes the image of $L$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ pointwise, for all $x', y' \in Pl$ with $x'y' = (\rho(\varpi))^e$ and with $\tau(x')\tau(y') = (\rho(\varpi))^e$ as well (where $\tau$ acts on $Pl$ through the ring homomorphism `MulSemiringAction.toRingHom`), and for any two morphisms $s, s' : \operatorname{Spec} Pl \to U$ which are sections of the projection (i.e. $s$, resp. $s'$, followed by $U \hookrightarrow$ base change followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} Pl$ is the identity) such that $s'$ followed by $U \hookrightarrow$ base change followed by the projection to the two-chart model equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\tau)$ followed by the corresponding composite for $s$: if $s$ followed by $f$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the homomorphism `CrossingQuotient.lift` determined by the pair $(x', y')$, then $s'$ followed by $f$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the homomorphism `CrossingQuotient.lift` determined by $(\tau(x'), \tau(y'))$ (the lift sending the two coordinates to the given pair with product $(\rho(\varpi))^e$).
--
--   (6) For every $y \in U$ with `CrossingQuotient.V ((ρ ϖ) ^ e)` in $f(y)$, the image of $y$ lies in the image of $i_1$ followed by $bc$.
--
--   (7) For every $y \in U$ with `CrossingQuotient.U ((ρ ϖ) ^ e)` in $f(y)$, the image of $y$ lies in the image of $i_2$ followed by $bc$.
--
--   (8) Conversely, for every $y \in U$ whose image lies in the image of $i_1$ followed by $bc$, `CrossingQuotient.V ((ρ ϖ) ^ e)` lies in $f(y)$.
--
--   (9) For every $y \in U$ whose image lies in the image of $i_2$ followed by $bc$, `CrossingQuotient.U ((ρ ϖ) ^ e)` lies in $f(y)$.
--
--   The exponent $e$ is the same over $Pl$ as over $O$.
--
--   This transports an oriented étale crossing chart at a point $\nu$ of the intersection of the two components $C_1, C_2$ of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ from the intermediate coefficient ring $O$ to the valuation subring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $p$, retaining the vertex, flatness, residue and étaleness conditions and the orientation, and gaining equivariance for the inertia at $Pl$ acting trivially on $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart_valuationSubring_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart_valuationSubring_twoChartModel_x1_mul), in the analysis of the semistable reduction of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$.
